---
// What OpenWren does not do, said the same way on every page that compares or sells it.
---

<ul>
  <li><strong>No Microsoft 365, Exchange or Outlook.com accounts yet.</strong> OpenWren works with Gmail and with any account that offers IMAP and a password or app password.</li>
  <li><strong>No calendar or contacts manager.</strong> It is a mail program only.</li>
  <li><strong>No POP3</strong>, and no built-in PGP or S/MIME encryption of messages.</li>
  <li><strong>It is young.</strong> The first version came out in November 2026, and it is made by one person.</li>
</ul>
